# 🚆 IRCTC Case Study — User Persona

## Proposed RailEase User Persona

### Name
Rahul Sharma

### Age
28

### Occupation
Working Professional

### Location
Delhi NCR

### Travel Pattern
- Frequently travels by train
- Mostly takes long-distance journeys
- Occasionally travels overnight
- Uses Tatkal when required
- Usually books tickets online

---

## Goals

Rahul wants to:

- Book a train ticket quickly
- Find the right train and seat easily
- Complete payment without uncertainty
- Avoid repeated login or OTP problems
- Know whether his ticket is successfully booked
- Get clear information when something goes wrong

---

## Frustrations

Rahul becomes frustrated when:

- The website/app takes too long to load
- The service becomes unavailable
- The server is busy during Tatkal
- He gets logged out unexpectedly
- OTPs are delayed
- Seat availability changes while booking
- Payment status is unclear
- An error occurs without clear instructions

---

## Behaviour

- Primarily uses IRCTC website and Rail Connect
- Checks train availability before booking
- Tries to book as soon as Tatkal opens when necessary
- May switch between website and app when facing problems
- Relies on online booking because visiting a ticket counter is inconvenient

---

## Needs

Rahul needs:

1. Fast access during booking
2. Reliable booking flow
3. Clear seat availability
4. Simple authentication
5. Clear payment/booking status
6. Helpful error messages
7. Easy recovery when something goes wrong

---

## Key Quote

> "I just want to know whether my ticket is booked or not."

---

## Core User Need

**Rahul needs a fast, reliable and transparent booking experience so that he can complete his journey planning without uncertainty or unnecessary stress.**

---

## Research Basis

This persona is based on patterns observed in the initial RailEase user research survey.

The persona is a representation of a user segment and does not represent one specific survey respondent.

As more survey responses are collected, this persona will be validated and refined.
